<title>SINGAPORE: United Overseas Land 1996 net up 27 pct.</title>
<headline>United Overseas Land 1996 net up 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	    (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  64.43     vs    50.77</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	     12.70     vs    10.20</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		 7.50     vs     7.50</p>
<p>    Turnover			   311.69     vs   232.69</p>
<p>    Investment income		 16.28     vs    24.55</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  34.01     vs    32.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    78.14     vs    70.15</p>
<p>    Associates			  (2.46)    vs    (0.22)</p>
<p>    Tax				    7.21     vs    18.01</p>
<p>    Minorities			  (4.05)    vs    (1.16)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		    5.49     vs     5.70</p>
<p>Dividend register - June 4 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name is United Overseas Land Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
